# @@STACK@@

The shared RDS Postgres instance (@@DATABASE_CLASS@@, @@STORAGE_GB@@ GB, Postgres @@ENGINE_VERSION@@, @@BACKUP_DAYS@@-day backups) on which several
sites each keep their own database and login role. Generated by `hecks deploy project`; do not edit `rds.yaml`.

## Create it

```
make stack VPC=vpc-... PRIVATE_SUBNETS=subnet-a,subnet-b BASTION_SG=sg-... ALERT_EMAIL=you@example.com
```

`BASTION_SG` is the security group of the machine that tunnels to the instance over SSM (a site's own box works).
Outputs: `DbEndpoint`, `DbSecurityGroupId`, `DbSecretArn` (the master secret) and `AlertTopicArn`.

## Add a site

A site's world says `shared_database "@@STACK@@"`. Its generated `provision-database.sh` creates that site's role, its
database, and the secret `<site>/database` that its containers read; its box stack adds its own ingress rule to this
instance's security group. Nothing else needs to change here.

## Things to know

- The master secret is read only by the person who provisions a site, never by a box.
- This stack cannot be deleted while any site's box stack still references its security group.
- One maintenance window, restart or failure touches every site. Alarms (storage, CPU, memory) are for the instance.
